  {kind="narration",pos=273.613,dur=6.711,name="NARRATION 014 | And like me, she had no idea how much that trust would eve",text="And like me, she had no idea how much that trust would eventually cost her.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=90},
  {kind="narration",pos=280.624,dur=21.791,name="NARRATION 015 | When Angela turned on us in September, I started going thr",text="When Angela turned on us in September, I started going through the recordings from thirty-five public broadcasts and the private messages behind them. I also started talking to the people Angela had been close to before us—people whose warnings I had dismissed when Angela and I were still on good terms.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=92},
  {kind="narration",pos=302.715,dur=6.306,name="NARRATION 016 | And as I laid the recordings out in chronological order, t",text="And as I laid the recordings out in chronological order, two things became clear.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=94},
  {kind="narration",pos=309.321,dur=23.413,name="NARRATION 017 | First, what happened to Sav and me wasn't a one-off argume",text="First, what happened to Sav and me wasn't a one-off argument. Multiple former friends and associates across the community described the same experience: trusting Angela as a friend and advocate, confiding private struggles or family details to her, and later watching those confidences used to humiliate, intimidate, or retaliate against them when the relationship soured.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=96},
  {kind="narration",pos=333.033,dur=15.63,name="NARRATION 018 | And second: whenever Angela's conduct was challenged, she ",text="And second: whenever Angela's conduct was challenged, she had a story ready to explain why *she* was actually the victim—why she had been silenced, cornered, or forced to act in order to protect someone else.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=98},
  {kind="archive_angela",pos=348.963,dur=10.0,name="ARCHIVE C10 AQ-0027 | 010__AQ-0027__Collecting_NDAs_Act_Accordingly.wav",text="Manuscript line 99\n[CLIP #002-P | AQ-0027 | *Logan Black Unmasked* (20260918_1MJgNbdaAPlGL), Sept 18, 2026, 01:59:56]\nManifest status: existing\nAudio cut boundaries/context and speaker NOT independently verified. Audition before publication.\nOriginal source: C:\\Users\\Logan\\Downloads\\sav\\angela\\21_Collecting_NDAs_Act_Accordingly.wav",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\papertrail_archival_audio_ordered\\010__AQ-0027__Collecting_NDAs_Act_Accordingly.wav",status="existing",line=99},
  {kind="narration",pos=359.243,dur=18.142,name="NARRATION 019 | Because Angela recorded herself talking for hundreds of ho",text="Because Angela recorded herself talking for hundreds of hours across public rooms, we don't have to take her explanations at face value. We can test what she claimed against what she actually said, what she admitted doing, and what the record shows.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=106},
  {kind="narration",pos=377.686,dur=5.82,name="NARRATION 020 | In fact, Angela gave the audience her own invitation to do",text="In fact, Angela gave the audience her own invitation to do exactly that:",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=108},
