  {kind="sfx",pos=466.571,dur=0.12,name="SFX 08 | SFX: Subtle, dry X Space room ambiance—the faint click of a microphone unm",text="SFX: Subtle, dry X Space room ambiance—the faint click of a microphone unmuting, then resting beneath Logan's voice.",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\THE_PAPER_TRAIL_REAPER_ASSEMBLY_20261112\\SCRATCH_phone_send_click.wav",status="SCRATCH - replace before release",line=136},
  {kind="narration",pos=466.571,dur=12.387,name="NARRATION 023 | If you've never spent time in an X Space late at night, th",text="If you've never spent time in an X Space late at night, the easiest way to picture it is an open phone line that never really hangs up.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=140},
  {kind="narration",pos=479.258,dur=32.086,name="NARRATION 024 | Somebody's sitting in a parked car after a night shift. So",text="Somebody's sitting in a parked car after a night shift. Somebody else is folding laundry in their living room or walking the dog at two in the morning. A dozen people might be listening, or a few hundred. The title on the screen might say UFO disclosure or government corruption, but within twenty minutes, people are talking about their divorces, their kids, their money troubles, or the worst thing that ever happened to them growing up.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=142},
  {kind="narration",pos=511.644,dur=10.034,name="NARRATION 025 | You hear the same voices night after night. And before lon",text="You hear the same voices night after night. And before long, you feel like you know people you've never laid eyes on.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=144},
  {kind="direction",pos=521.978,dur=0.5,name="PAUSE | [beat]",text="[beat]",path="",status="TIMING GUIDE",line=145},
  {kind="narration",pos=522.478,dur=5.9,name="NARRATION 026 | That was the world where I first met Angela back in late 2",text="That was the world where I first met Angela back in late 2023.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=148},
  {kind="narration",pos=528.678,dur=12.061,name="NARRATION 027 | When she came up to the microphone, she spoke using her re",text="When she came up to the microphone, she spoke using her real name, from North Carolina, near Fort Bragg. And she told a story that stopped rooms cold.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=150},
  {kind="archive_angela",pos=541.04,dur=42.0,name="ARCHIVE C13 AQ-0115 | 013__AQ-0115__Quote_05_Kidnapped_As_A_Baby.mp3",text="Manuscript line 151\n[CLIP #115-A | AQ-0115 | *Blame Mellow Demon* (20260218_1YpKkgYPjkmKj), Feb 18, 2026]\nManifest status: existing\nAudio cut boundaries/context and speaker NOT independently verified. Audition before publication.\nOriginal source: C:\\Users\\Logan\\Downloads\\sav\\angela\\Quote_05_Kidnapped_As_A_Baby.mp3",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\papertrail_archival_audio_ordered\\013__AQ-0115__Quote_05_Kidnapped_As_A_Baby.mp3",status="existing",line=151},
  {kind="sfx",pos=583.32,dur=3.0,name="SFX 09 | SFX: Clip fades cleanly. Silence: 1 beat.",text="SFX: Clip fades cleanly. Silence: 1 beat.",path="",status="CUE ONLY - AUDIO NOT SELECTED",line=156},
  {kind="narration",pos=583.32,dur=25.44,name="NARRATION 028 | In other recordings, Angela described further experiences ",text="In other recordings, Angela described further experiences that I cannot independently verify. She claimed she had been illegally adopted into a CIA mind-control program (`AQ-0011`), tortured as a child at Wright-Patterson Air Force Base, and that she had personally helped law enforcement track down a kidnapped thirteen-year-old girl in New York using only a first name and an Xbox account (`AQ-0195`).",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=160},
  {kind="narration",pos=609.059,dur=15.71,name="NARRATION 029 | Later on, some of her former friends would allege on the r",text="Later on, some of her former friends would allege on the record that she fabricated key parts of her personal history (`AQ-0206`, `AQ-0209`). Angela insisted every word was real and dared critics to prove her wrong (`AQ-0056`).",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=162},
  {kind="narration",pos=625.069,dur=36.871,name="NARRATION 030 | When I first got to know her, I was not investigating her ",text="When I first got to know her, I was not investigating her childhood. Someone says they survived something awful and want to protect children, and your instinct in a late-night conversation is to listen. And when Angela talked about why she kept meticulous notes on everyone and everything in her life, she gave an explanation that made you feel sympathy for her: she said her father had taught her as a little girl to keep a hidden journal so she could survive her abusers and beat them in court.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=164},
