  {kind="narration",pos=2496.37,dur=4.279,name="NARRATION 105 | “A long line of destruction behind me for accountability.”",text="“A long line of destruction behind me for accountability.”",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=489},
  {kind="narration",pos=2500.948,dur=17.412,name="NARRATION 106 | I can't confirm the jail time or the confiscated firearms ",text="I can't confirm the jail time or the confiscated firearms from this recording. But I don't have to guess how Angela wanted the audience to understand her actions. She used the word *destruction* herself—and placed it under *accountability*.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=491},
  {kind="narration",pos=2518.66,dur=10.034,name="NARRATION 107 | In another confrontation, she went beyond describing claim",text="In another confrontation, she went beyond describing claimed consequences. Somebody asked her directly whether she had helped disclose other people's private information.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=493},
  {kind="archive_angela",pos=2528.994,dur=32.0,name="ARCHIVE C37 AQ-0134 | 040__AQ-0134__Quote_07_Shane_I_Did_Do_That.mp3",text="Manuscript line 494\n[CLIP #134 | *Angela Maggard Fan Club* (20260918_1AxRnZMeZNYxl), Sept 18, 2026, 01:14:02]\nManifest status: existing\nAudio cut boundaries/context and speaker NOT independently verified. Audition before publication.\nOriginal source: C:\\Users\\Logan\\Downloads\\sav\\angela\\Quote_07_Shane_I_Did_Do_That.mp3",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\papertrail_archival_audio_ordered\\040__AQ-0134__Quote_07_Shane_I_Did_Do_That.mp3",status="existing",line=494},
  {kind="narration",pos=2561.274,dur=1.9,name="NARRATION 108 | “I absolutely did.”",text="“I absolutely did.”",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=501},
  {kind="narration",pos=2563.474,dur=10.114,name="NARRATION 109 | Angela said people had sent her the information to provoke",text="Angela said people had sent her the information to provoke her. That was her explanation. But she'd just acknowledged her own participation.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=503},
  {kind="narration",pos=2573.889,dur=15.305,name="NARRATION 110 | When former friends accused her of exposing private inform",text="When former friends accused her of exposing private information, I had only their testimony. Here, I could hear Angela accept responsibility for helping expose it—though not proof that she was responsible for every other allegation.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=505},
  {kind="narration",pos=2589.493,dur=7.927,name="NARRATION 111 | And one of the people who had trusted Angela with painful ",text="And one of the people who had trusted Angela with painful details of her own life was Sav.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=507},
  {kind="narration",pos=2598.22,dur=3.873,name="NARRATION 112 | Go back to August, before the September broadcasts.",text="Go back to August, before the September broadcasts.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=514},
  {kind="narration",pos=2602.394,dur=17.737,name="NARRATION 113 | Sav was already going through a separation and trying to k",text="Sav was already going through a separation and trying to keep a home for her children. She had trusted Angela with the parts of her life she wasn't comfortable discussing in public—including arguments and insecurities in her relationship with me.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=516},
  {kind="narration",pos=2620.431,dur=13.358,name="NARRATION 114 | According to Sav, the immediate crisis began when Angela s",text="According to Sav, the immediate crisis began when Angela shared screenshots Sav had specifically asked her not to send. That triggered a fight between Sav and me. We blocked each other.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=518},
  {kind="narration",pos=2634.088,dur=12.952,name="NARRATION 115 | Sav was overwhelmed. She was crying and sending incoherent",text="Sav was overwhelmed. She was crying and sending incoherent messages in a group chat with Angela and their friend Sara Beth. She also made alarming statements about ending her life.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=520},
  {kind="narration",pos=2647.34,dur=7.522,name="NARRATION 116 | Sav has acknowledged that those words were serious and tha",text="Sav has acknowledged that those words were serious and that she shouldn't have used them lightly.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=522},
  {kind="narration",pos=2655.162,dur=11.251,name="NARRATION 117 | She called Sara Beth to calm down. Sav says Sara Beth help",text="She called Sara Beth to calm down. Sav says Sara Beth helped her through the panic, and that both of them told Angela she was okay.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=524},
  {kind="narration",pos=2666.713,dur=16.601,name="NARRATION 118 | Angela nonetheless believed a police welfare check was nec",text="Angela nonetheless believed a police welfare check was necessary. While I was at work, Sara Beth asked me for Sav's address on Angela's behalf. I gave it to her because I wanted to know Sav was safe.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=526},
  {kind="narration",pos=2683.614,dur=14.414,name="NARRATION 119 | When Sara Beth told Sav that a welfare check was being cal",text="When Sara Beth told Sav that a welfare check was being called, Sav says she was overwhelmed again—after the friend she'd called for help had already talked her through the initial panic.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=528},
  {kind="narration",pos=2698.328,dur=9.224,name="NARRATION 120 | She still had children in the house. She needed them to kn",text="She still had children in the house. She needed them to know what was about to happen without frightening them more.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=530},
  {kind="narration",pos=2707.851,dur=10.765,name="NARRATION 121 | In a written statement she provided for this documentary, ",text="In a written statement she provided for this documentary, Sav described what that moment felt like. These are her words, read aloud from the statement:",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=532},
  {kind="reading",pos=2718.916,dur=29.676,name="WRITTEN READING 001 | \"I basically had the biggest panic attack after she told m",text="\"I basically had the biggest panic attack after she told me Angela was calling a wellfare check after we had told her Sarah was able to calm me down from one of the worst panic attacks I’ve had. I collected myself and then told my kids that a police officer would be stopping by and that everything would be okay to just go play upstairs they wouldn’t be there long.\"",path="",status="RECORDING REQUIRED",line=535},
  {kind="narration",pos=2748.892,dur=8.007,name="NARRATION 122 | Sav says she spoke to the officer with Sara Beth still on ",text="Sav says she spoke to the officer with Sara Beth still on the phone. Then the police left.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=538},
  {kind="narration",pos=2757.199,dur=16.681,name="NARRATION 123 | We have to keep two questions separate. Was a check reason",text="We have to keep two questions separate. Was a check reasonable after a message suggesting someone might end their life? It could have been. Angela has said she was afraid for Sav and knew calling might cost their friendship.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=540},
  {kind="narration",pos=2774.18,dur=16.926,name="NARRATION 124 | But Sav says the call went ahead after both she and Sara B",text="But Sav says the call went ahead after both she and Sara Beth told Angela she had calmed down. Sav believed the way it was handled was connected to the online dispute, and that she was being taught a lesson.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=542},
  {kind="narration",pos=2791.406,dur=7.602,name="NARRATION 125 | That is Sav's interpretation. I cannot know Angela's priva",text="That is Sav's interpretation. I cannot know Angela's private motive from the accounts we have.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=544},
  {kind="narration",pos=2799.308,dur=10.034,name="NARRATION 126 | What I can do is follow what happened to information from ",text="What I can do is follow what happened to information from that night. Because the story didn't end when the officer left.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=546},
  {kind="narration",pos=2809.642,dur=12.061,name="NARRATION 127 | Within weeks, Angela was describing disappointment with pe",text="Within weeks, Angela was describing disappointment with people she considered friends. On September 7, she named Sine and me while explaining why she believed others had failed her.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=548},
  {kind="archive_angela",pos=2822.004,dur=36.53,name="ARCHIVE C38 AQ-0175 | 041__AQ-0175__Crackheads_Predators_No.wav",text="Manuscript line 549\n[CLIP #175-A | AQ-0175 | *CRACKHEADS TAKING OVER DISCLOSURE* (20260907_1OxwbneDwBqJB), Sept 7, 2026]\nManifest status: existing\nAudio cut boundaries/context and speaker NOT independently verified. Audition before publication.\nOriginal source: C:\\Users\\Logan\\OneDrive\\Documents\\AngelaMaster\\media\\AQ-0175_Angela.wav",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\papertrail_archival_audio_ordered\\041__AQ-0175__Crackheads_Predators_No.wav",status="existing",line=549},
  {kind="narration",pos=2858.814,dur=9.954,name="NARRATION 128 | The next day, on September 8, Angela began a broadcast in ",text="The next day, on September 8, Angela began a broadcast in which she announced that she was going to post private relationship messages.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=556},
  {kind="narration",pos=2869.068,dur=7.116,name="NARRATION 129 | And that is where the personal crisis Sav had described be",text="And that is where the personal crisis Sav had described became part of something much bigger.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=558},
  {kind="narration",pos=2877.484,dur=9.629,name="NARRATION 130 | By the beginning of September, private conversations were ",text="By the beginning of September, private conversations were already making their way into public Spaces. And people were nervous about getting involved.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=567},
  {kind="narration",pos=2887.413,dur=12.467,name="NARRATION 131 | The Space was what the audience heard. The back channels—p",text="The Space was what the audience heard. The back channels—private messages, group chats, and Discord rooms—were where people said things they never expected that audience to hear.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=569},
  {kind="narration",pos=2900.18,dur=15.385,name="NARRATION 132 | On September 2, I talked about screenshots I believed Ange",text="On September 2, I talked about screenshots I believed Angela had posted. I asked another host to hide them. He wouldn't—and the reason he gave says something about how powerful her reputation had become.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=571},
  {kind="narration",pos=2915.865,dur=11.171,name="NARRATION 133 | You'll hear his refusal described in my own words, followe",text="You'll hear his refusal described in my own words, followed by another speaker who starts to explain why he wanted no part of the conflict.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=573},
  {kind="archive_other",pos=2927.335,dur=30.6,name="ARCHIVE C39 AQ-0278 | 042a__AQ-0278__Logan_Archival_Comments.wav",text="Manuscript line 574\n[CLIP #029-M & #030-M | AQ-0278 & AQ-0279 | *Bidets the day* (20260902_1qGvvevyVvgGB), Sept 2, 2026, 385.0s]\nManifest status: existing\nAudio cut boundaries/context and speaker NOT independently verified. Audition before publication.\nOriginal source: c:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\special_clips\\Cue_01_AQ-0278_Logan_Black.wav",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\papertrail_archival_audio_ordered\\042a__AQ-0278__Logan_Archival_Comments.wav",status="existing",line=574},
  {kind="archive_other",pos=2958.215,dur=5.7,name="ARCHIVE C39 AQ-0279 | 042b__AQ-0279__Community_Witness_Reaction.wav",text="Manuscript line 574\n[CLIP #029-M & #030-M | AQ-0278 & AQ-0279 | *Bidets the day* (20260902_1qGvvevyVvgGB), Sept 2, 2026, 385.0s]\nManifest status: existing\nAudio cut boundaries/context and speaker NOT independently verified. Audition before publication.\nOriginal source: c:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\special_clips\\Cue_01_AQ-0279_Speaker_3_Community_.wav",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\papertrail_archival_audio_ordered\\042b__AQ-0279__Community_Witness_Reaction.wav",status="existing",line=574},
  {kind="narration",pos=2964.195,dur=4.199,name="NARRATION 134 | “Because they told her secrets and they can never—”",text="“Because they told her secrets and they can never—”",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=580},
  {kind="narration",pos=2968.694,dur=9.304,name="NARRATION 135 | He stops there. The rest of that thought isn't recorded. B",text="He stops there. The rest of that thought isn't recorded. But the fear in the conversation is hard to miss.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=582},
  {kind="narration",pos=2978.297,dur=16.115,name="NARRATION 136 | By then, even other hosts were afraid of what might happen",text="By then, even other hosts were afraid of what might happen if they crossed Angela. Six days later, something happened in my own room that Angela would use to explain why she was releasing even more private messages.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=584},
  {kind="narration",pos=2994.713,dur=23.573,name="NARRATION 137 | On September 8, Oor—a man involved in a bitter feud with A",text="On September 8, Oor—a man involved in a bitter feud with Angela—made a cruel remark about her deceased baby in a Space I was hosting. Sav was listening. According to her message to Angela, I immediately warned Oor to stop and removed him from the panel. Angela later acknowledged that I'd done so.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=586},
  {kind="narration",pos=3018.585,dur=13.683,name="NARRATION 138 | Nothing excuses what Oor said. Yet Angela went on to cite ",text="Nothing excuses what Oor said. Yet Angela went on to cite what happened in my room when she announced a broadcast devoted to exposing private messages from Sav's and my relationship.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=588},
  {kind="narration",pos=3032.568,dur=5.98,name="NARRATION 139 | It was called *Petty Space*. She was about to publish scre",text="It was called *Petty Space*. She was about to publish screenshots in batches.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=590},
  {kind="archive_angela",pos=3038.849,dur=56.2,name="ARCHIVE C40 AQ-0261 | 043a__AQ-0261__Monologue_Of_Truth.wav",text="Manuscript line 591\n[CLIP #104 & #105 | AQ-0261 & AQ-0262 | *Petty Space* (20260908_1wxWjlrwXokJQ), Sept 8, 2026, 4.1s & 113.9s]\nManifest status: existing\nAudio cut boundaries/context and speaker NOT independently verified. Audition before publication.\nOriginal source: C:\\Users\\Logan\\OneDrive\\Documents\\AngelaMaster\\media\\AQ-0261_Angela_Maggard.wav",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\papertrail_archival_audio_ordered\\043a__AQ-0261__Monologue_Of_Truth.wav",status="existing",line=591},
  {kind="archive_angela",pos=3095.329,dur=41.4,name="ARCHIVE C40 AQ-0262 | 043b__AQ-0262__Receipts_Documentation.wav",text="Manuscript line 591\n[CLIP #104 & #105 | AQ-0261 & AQ-0262 | *Petty Space* (20260908_1wxWjlrwXokJQ), Sept 8, 2026, 4.1s & 113.9s]\nManifest status: existing\nAudio cut boundaries/context and speaker NOT independently verified. Audition before publication.\nOriginal source: C:\\Users\\Logan\\OneDrive\\Documents\\AngelaMaster\\media\\AQ-0262_Angela_Maggard.wav",path="C:\\Users\\Logan\\copy-spaces-to-youtube-pipeline\\papertrail_archival_audio_ordered\\043b__AQ-0262__Receipts_Documentation.wav",status="existing",line=591},
  {kind="narration",pos=3137.009,dur=14.819,name="NARRATION 140 | Picture what that means for the person whose messages are ",text="Picture what that means for the person whose messages are being read: something said in a moment of insecurity or anger, which was never meant for strangers, now becoming the subject of a live broadcast.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=596},
  {kind="narration",pos=3152.128,dur=12.141,name="NARRATION 141 | Angela said she was exposing abusive behavior. That was he",text="Angela said she was exposing abusive behavior. That was her public explanation. Sav said she had confided those messages to a friend and didn't want them released.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=598},
  {kind="narration",pos=3164.569,dur=6.306,name="NARRATION 142 | Angela also described how she would keep more information ",text="Angela also described how she would keep more information in reserve until people responded.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=600},
  {kind="narration",pos=3171.175,dur=11.736,name="NARRATION 143 | This is what she said after one of the batches. The laught",text="This is what she said after one of the batches. The laughter is directed at me. But the private information making that moment possible came from Sav.",path="",status="NARRATION RECORDING REQUIRED",line=602},
